-- Catalog avatars for roster units (client visuals only), keyed by unit id (UnitConfig key). A unit
-- with catalog items is drawn as a blocky R6 avatar wearing them instead of its hand-built look
-- (UnitLookConfig) or placeholder. The server builds each avatar once at start
-- (src/server/AvatarService.luau) and shares it; the client poses it like any figure (Figure).
-- If an item fails or the avatar takes too long to load, the unit keeps its usual figure and the
-- server warns once, naming the unit and the asset. Display names stay in SkinConfig.
--
-- Two sources, merged per unit into `units`:
--   UnitAvatarPicks  the catalog items (generated by scripts/catalog-apply.luau from the picker
--                    page, docs/references/catalog/index.html): accessories { { slot, id } },
--                    shirt, pants, face. Only units with picks are avatars.
--   `tuning` below   hand-tuned fields, kept across applies (a field here wins over a pick):
--     skin         body color for every limb (default `defaultSkin`); `colors` { head, torso,
--                  leftArm, rightArm, leftLeg, rightLeg } overrides single limbs
--     scale        size multiplier (as FigureConfig.characters `scale`; presentation only)
--     prop         true: also hold the class prop (FigureConfig.classes) in the hands. Off by
--                  default: avatars carry their own weapons instead of the placeholder props.
--     weapons      LookKit weapons (UnitLookConfig `weapons` format) worn with the avatar. Default:
--                  the unit's UnitLookConfig weapons, if it has a hand-built look; false: none.
--                  A weapon may also ride another anchor: `anchor` ("head", "hips" ...) with `at`
--                  (height fractions) and `turn` (degrees) setting its grip. On an avatar, katana,
--                  dagger and greatsword hilts default longer so they show past the blocky fist.
--                  `drawn = true`: the weapon shows only while attacking or casting (a quick-draw).
--     hand, arms   attack hand ("left", "right", "both") and resting arm angles { left, right }
--                  in degrees, replacing the class's (presentation only)
--     outfit       block-built pieces layered on the avatar (LookKit, UnitLookConfig fields: coat,
--                  collar, belt, sash, scarf, tie, cravat, buttons, bands, emblems, gearBoxes,
--                  tendrils, extras, and `hair` / `headwear` sized to the R6 head) for what the
--                  catalog items lack. Default: the unit's UnitLookConfig tendrils, if any.
-- A unit may have no shirt and/or no pants: Roblox adds no clothing then; its limbs show `colors`.
-- Outfit sizes and positions are fractions of the figure's height on the R6 body: torso 0.4 wide,
-- 0.4 tall and 0.2 deep (front at -0.1), limbs 0.2 thick, legs and arms 0.4 long; the head about
-- 0.25 across.
-- R6 renders classic clothing and rigid accessories, not layered clothing.

local UnitAvatarPicks = require(script.Parent.UnitAvatarPicks)

